    "_postman_id": "b8d3ba59-1b5e-4303-be3c-956ac6459297",
    "name": "Morrow API",
    "description": "# Morrow API\n\nREST API for a shared personal calendar. Users can create calendars, invite other users to share them, and manage members and appointments.\n\n## Base URL\n\nAll requests use `{{base_url}}` (set in the `Morrow local` environment).\n\n## Authentication\n\nAuthentication uses Laravel Passport. Both endpoints return a JSON object with `user` and `token`. Register or log in to get an access token, then send it in every protected request:\n\n`` Authorization: Bearer `YOUR_TOKEN` ``\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Send `Accept: application/json` and `Content-Type: application/json` in every request.\n    \n- Common status codes: `200` OK, `201` Created, `401` Unauthenticated, `403` Forbidden, `404` Not found, `409` Conflict, `422` Validation error.\n    \n\n## Status\n\nDocumented so far: `POST /api/register`, `POST /api/login`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
